  "verbalization": "Regorafenib is classified as a Cytochrome P450 2c9 (CYP2C9) inhibitor, and this classification is supported by its inclusion in the list of inhibitors of this enzyme. The mechanism of action involves Regorafenib binding to Cyp2c8, as evidenced by the interaction between Zafirlukast and Cyp2c8 in Path 1, and between Amiodarone and Cyp2c8 in Path 2. The lowest common ancestor of Regorafenib and Zafirlukast is an Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound, while the lowest common ancestor of Regorafenib and Amiodarone is an Organic Heterocyclic Compound. These relationships suggest that Regorafenib may interact with Cyp2c8 through a common pathway, possibly involving the inhibition of CYP2C9, which is a key enzyme in drug metabolism. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Regorafenib to modulate CYP2C9 activity, contributing to its pharmacological effects.",
